1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:10,260
That is secondary growth: the increase in thickness of a stem or root, made by two lateral meristems, the vascular cambium and the cork cambium.

2
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:13,281
It happens in dicots and gymnosperms.

3
00:00:13,281 --> 00:00:17,213
Monocots normally do not have it, and leaves never do.

